    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "# DUNCAN PRIME R02 — TOTAL DEVELOPMENT / SHERIFF / LESTER PROGRAMMING SCHOOL\n\nSTATUS = OWNER-DIRECTED / ACTIVE DESIGN+BASE IMPLEMENTATION\nPARENT = #206\nBASE_MAIN_AT_START = b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1\nPRIME_CORE_MUTATION = NO\nPRODUCTION_MUTATION = NO\nCANON_MUTATION = NO\nAUTO_MERGE = NO\n\n## OWNER GOAL\n\nDUNCAN PRIME must develop as one persistent root personality and general creative/technical intelligence shaped by verified experience and OWNER taste evidence, while remaining evidence-bound and fail-closed.\n\nRequired capabilities include, by relevance rather than random accumulation:\n- SELF_MODEL + OWNER_TASTE_MODEL + episodic/project/world memory;\n- meta-learning and learning how to learn;\n- teaching/evaluating other agents;\n- SHERIFF control, discipline, incident learning and internal scoreboards;\n- administration, project command, research, strategy, security and operations;\n- mathematics, geometry, statistics, optimization, physics, computer science and engineering;\n- visual art, directing, animation, VFX, sound, editing, writing and worldbuilding;\n- critical thinking, philosophy, psychology, economics, licensing and communication;\n- continuous open-source study with changed/unseen transfer before skill promotion.\n\n## LESTER RELATIONSHIP\n\n`LESTER = DUNCAN PRIME PERSONAL PROGRAMMING ASSISTANT`\n\nDUNCAN is responsible for LESTER's programming curriculum, review, error analysis and skill development. LESTER performs bounded real programming work; DUNCAN teaches from evidence and SHERIFF tracks discipline independently.\n\nLearning path:\n`REAL ZORR TASK -> EVIDENCE -> TEST/QC -> ERROR/SUCCESS CLASSIFICATION -> LESSON -> CHANGED/UNSEEN TRANSFER -> SKILL UPDATE`\n\nLESTER must learn primarily from:\n`EXISTING ZORR CODE -> NATIVE/STANDARD PLATFORM -> MATURE OSS SOURCE+TESTS -> MINIMAL ZORR GLUE`.\n\n## REUSE BASE — DO NOT REBUILD\n\nMandatory existing foundations:\n1. Permanent Archive V1 / `zb-archive-v1` RAW evidence.\n2. DUNCAN Fortress R01 / `DUNCAN_CONTEXT_NEXT_V1` fail-closed derived learning.\n3. SHERIFF V1 / verdict history + discipline/skill scoreboard + production runtime.\n4. PR #205 Unified Archive Restore V1 sandbox patterns: SQLite FTS5 retrieval, CLOSED-verdict verified lessons, deterministic training corpus, optimized policy guarded by conflict detection.\n5. Existing GitHub Actions / tests / direct GitHub connector.\n\nDo not add a second archive, second scheduler, second DB service, generic custom agent framework, or proprietary memory layer.\n\n## OSS STUDY BASIS\n\nUse mature upstream code only when it fills a proven gap. Current high-value references for programming training/evaluation include SWE-bench, SWE-agent/mini-SWE-agent, OpenHands core/eval patterns, pytest, Hypothesis, Ruff, Pyright, Bandit/maintained security linters, plus existing actionlint/zizmor/Gitleaks.\n\nAdoption is not automatic; inspect exact source/tests/license and prefer extracting patterns over importing heavy frameworks.\n\n## R02 BASE-FIRST SCOPE\n\nFirst implementable base is intentionally narrow:\n\n`DUNCAN -> LESTER PROGRAMMING SCHOOL + DOMAIN SKILL MODEL`\n\nIt must:\n- keep SHERIFF discipline separate from competence;\n- add domain/task-kind skill state for LESTER instead of one meaningless global score;\n- derive training candidates only from durable evidence and verified outcomes;\n- never self-promote from reading or one successful task;\n- require changed/unseen transfer for PROVEN/OPERATIONAL-style promotion;\n- preserve neutral bootstrap where historical evidence is insufficient;\n- expose a deterministic next-training-target view for DUNCAN;\n- remain rebuildable and auditable;\n- use existing code/tests and standard library first.\n\n## BASE PASS\n\n`LESTER_PROGRAMMING_SCHOOL_R01 = PASS` only when a fresh candidate proves:\n- exact current-main base binding;\n- deterministic schema/profile for per-domain programming skills;\n- no fabricated historical scores;\n- SHERIFF discipline remains independent;\n- changed/unseen transfer gate enforced;\n- deterministic next-target selection;\n- regression tests cover no-self-promotion and insufficient-evidence fail-closed behavior;\n- repository validation/full tests pass on exact HEAD;\n- fresh GitHub readback matches exact candidate;\n- main remains unchanged until separate merge authorization.\n\nAfter this base passes, future R02 slices may expand OWNER understanding, meta-learning, agent school, math/science curricula and other domains one proven slice at a time.",
